{{Quote|Oh, you know the Western Reaches. It's a big place. Lots and lots of planets.|An [[Imperial officer]], to [[Han Solo]]|<ref name="CYD:H&C" />}}
The '''Western Reaches''', also known as the '''Western Regions''', comprised an area of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Trkn">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> The Western Reaches overlapped with several other regions of the galaxy, including the [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Outer Rim">''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'' places [[Mustafar]] in the Western Reaches. ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'' places Mustafar in the Atravis sector and denotes this sector as also belonging to the [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Therefore, some areas of the Outer Rim overlap with the Western Reaches.</ref> the [[Mid Rim Territories]].<ref name="TFA VD" />

==History==
After the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Galactic Empire]] initiated a [[Pacification operations in the Western Reaches|campaign]] against [[Separatist holdouts]] in the region, which would continue until the fourth [[Standard year|year]] of its [[Imperial Era|reign]]. [[Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] took part in these campaigns, removed from the media controversy over his role in the [[Antar Atrocity]]. After being reassigned to the remote Imperial facility known as [[Sentinel Base]], one false rumor spread that he had been given such an apparently insignificant posting because of a failure while commanding an important operation in the Western Reaches.<ref name="Trkn" />

After [[Captain]] [[Han Solo]] lost ownership of the [[freighter]] ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' to<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref> his hired hand<ref name="Grand Theft Falcon">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=18|story=Flight of the Falcon, Part 5: Grand Theft Falcon}}</ref> [[Gannis Ducain]], who would in turn lose possession of the [[starship]] to [[Vanver Irving|Vanver]] and [[Toursant Irving]], who themselves then lost it to the [[junk boss]] [[Unkar Plutt]],<ref name="Episode VII" /> Solo enlisted the help of<ref name="RevealHuntFalcon">{{WebCite|url=https://www.gamesradar.com/comics/marvel-comics/new-star-wars-comic-brings-han-solo-and-chewbacca-out-of-retirement-to-reclaim-the-millennium-falcon-in-the-time-between-return-of-the-jedi-and-the-force-awakens|text=New Star Wars comic brings Han Solo and Chewbacca out of retirement to reclaim the Millennium Falcon in the time between Return of the Jedi and The Force Awakens|archivedate=20250616230951}}</ref> his close friend and long time [[First Mate]]<ref name="CelebrationSpecial">''[[Star Wars: A New Hope - The Official Celebration Special]]''</ref> [[Chewbacca]] in finding the vessel. Embarking on a hunt for the ''Falcon''<ref name="RevealHuntFalcon" /> while also continuing their careers as [[smuggler]]s out of the starship ''[[Eravana]]'', Solo and Chewbacca's search saw them look through the Western Reaches, but they ultimately moved on after failing to locate the ''Falcon''. All the same, Solo thought the two needed to double check the region and even told Chewbacca of his suspicion. Indeed, the ''Falcon'' sat in Plutt's possession on the Western Reaches world of Jakku until it was stolen by his former [[scavenger]] [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]], the defected [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtrooper]] [[Finn]], and [[Resistance]] [[astromech droid]] [[BB-8]]. Upon finally rediscovering the vessel in their hands and learning from Rey it had sat on Jakku, Solo reminded Chewbacca that he had wanted to look through the Western Reaches again.<ref name="Episode VII" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Told you we should have double-checked the Western Reaches.|Han Solo, to Chewbacca|<ref name="Episode VII" />}}
[[File:TheGalaxy-GEG.png|thumb|left|300px|The map as presented in ''The Galactic Explorer's Guide'']]
The Western Reaches was originally established to be a region of the galaxy in the ''[[Star Wars Legends]]'' sourcebook ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'' released in [[2008]] and written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="The Essential Atlas">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref> It was brought into [[canon]] by the [[2014]] novel [[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']], by author [[James Luceno]].<ref name="Trkn" /> 

A line of dialogue by Han Solo in {{Film|VII}} implies that Jakku is located in the [[Western Reaches/Legends|Western Reaches]]; however, later sources, such as the ''[[Star Wars: The Galactic Explorer's Guide]]'' and the [[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map]] instead place the Jakku system directly west of the [[Core Worlds]], far north of the Western Reaches as defined by ''The Galactic Explorer's Guide''. According to author [[Jason Fry]], ''The Galactic Explorer's Guide'' is mistaken and Jakku is, indeed, within the Western Reaches.<ref name="Fry">{{EmailCite|email=File:AtlasEmail-2025-08-31.png|creator=[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-08-31}}</ref>

